<title>UK: ING Barings adds Norilsk Nickel to RDC programme.</title>
<headline>ING Barings adds Norilsk Nickel to RDC programme.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>ING Barings said on Wednesday that it has added Norilsk Nickel to its Russian Depositary Certificate programme.</p>
<p>Each RDC in Norilsk represents 1,000 underlying shares and is priced at the equivalent of $6.25/$6.50 per share.</p>
<p>The RDC programme, established in March last year, allows foreign investors to participate in Russian shares without local settlement and custody wrangles.</p>
<p>The Bank of Bermuda, which is custodian for the RDC programme has a sub-custody agreement with Russia's Uneximbank, which is an eligible custodian under U.S. SEC rules.</p>
<p>-- David Chance London newsroom 44 171 542 5887</p>
</text>
